            "text": "{\n  \"decision\": \"request_changes\",\n  \"thresholds_preserved\": true,\n  \"contradiction_requires_evidence\": true,\n  \"controls_consistent\": true,\n  \"reason\": \"The three-predicate definition is coherent: complete disclosures do not excuse an invented value, and a contradiction requires an identified claim and explicit conflicting evidence or report text. The documents also preserve the stated support, coverage, critical-error, disclosure, and failure-retention requirements, and correctly keep historical labels and results unchanged. However, the future validation path does not specify strong enough access and unblinding controls to demonstrate that held-out labels cannot leak into authoring, tuning, or evaluation, and the calibration gate is preserved by reference without its exact pass rule and denominator being stated.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"issue\": \"“Expected labels kept separate” and “blind contexts” do not specify who can access held-out reports and labels, when labels may be revealed, or how the held-out set is protected from iterative prompt/model selection. The plan also does not explicitly state whether the primary and secondary sets are disjoint or what each set is used for.\",\n      \"action\": \"Specify a holdout custodian and access boundary: keep labels and held-out references unavailable to report authors, prompt/model developers, and the model/judge; freeze and hash the complete evaluation packet before unblinding; state the roles of the primary and secondary sets and ensure they do not overlap. Make any post-unblinding changes a new version requiring a fresh held-out set.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"issue\": \"The plan says to retain the calibration gate and six frozen calibrations, but does not state the exact gate, scoring rule, denominator, or treatment of disagreements for the future protocol. That leaves room for an unintended gate change despite the preservation commitment.\",\n      \"action\": \"Record the exact calibration acceptance rule and denominator in the versioned protocol before evaluation, along with how uncertain or disputed ratings are handled. Keep the old v8 ratings and 2/3 failure unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"issue\": \"The proposed sample counts and threshold are stated, but the validation plan does not explain how the reported quality claim will be bounded to those specific reports and conditions.\",\n      \"action\":",
